  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\mathrm{n}$ is the number density and $\\mathrm{d}$ is the diameter of the molecule, then the average distance covered by a molecule between two successive collisions (i.e. mean free path) is represented by :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "T3JVi",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{n} \\pi \\mathrm{d}^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "UxqvF",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2 n \\pi d^2}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ItxHc",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2} n \\pi d^2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "X0xln",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2} n^2 \\pi^2 d^2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{n}=$ number of molecule per unit volume\n$\\mathrm{d}=$ diameter of the molecule\n$\\lambda=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2} \\pi \\mathrm{d}^2 \\mathrm{n}}$\n(By Theory)",
    "image": null
  },
